// Behavioural model of one LPDDR4 channel (x16) for simulation.
//
// Cycle-based: the model runs on a fast simulation clock `clk` (4 or more clocks per CK, an even
// number) and sees CK, CA, DQ and DQS as levels sampled on it. It checks what a controller and
// PHY can get wrong at the pins, and counts each error; it is not meant for synthesis.
//
// Commands (JESD209-4 SDR truth table, CA0 = LSB) are sampled on CK_t's rising edge; CS high
// marks the first cycle of a 2-cycle command. WR-1, RD-1, MRR-1 and MPC-1 (Read DQ Calibration)
// must be followed straight away by CAS-2, MRW-1 by MRW-2, ACT-1 by ACT-2. Timings are checked
// in CK cycles between the second cycles of the commands involved.
//
// Board: each byte lane's DQ, DMI and DQS from the controller side reach the DRAM
// WR_SKEWn_CLKS clocks later than CK, and its DQ WR_DQ_SKEWn_CLKS clocks later again. Write
// leveling and write DQ training are what take these out.
//
// Writes, per byte lane (Lpddr4WriteLane): the first data DQS_t rising edge must land in WL +
// tDQSS (0.75 to 1.25 tCK) after the CAS-2 edge, then 16 edges half a tCK (+-1 clock) apart with
// DQS_c the complement of DQS_t. Bursts may follow each other seamlessly (CAS-to-CAS = 8 tCK); up
// to four writes may be in flight. Each DQ must be driven and stable one clock either side of
// every edge; when one is not, the beat is taken anyway with that DQ's bit stored inverted (every
// bit when DQ is not driven), and the clock counts in `dq_viol` rather than in `errors`, so that
// write DQ training can sweep through failing delays, per lane or per DQ. A design must show no
// `dq_viol` once trained.
//
// VREF(DQ): MR14 sets the DQ input reference, at level 25 + OP5:0 (range 0, OP6 = 0) or
// 55 + OP5:0 (range 1) in 0.4 % of VDDQ steps. Outside VREF_OK_LO..VREF_OK_HI the write
// receivers lose a beat that differs from the one before it on its line: above the window a 1
// after a 0 is taken as 0, below it a 0 after a 1 is taken as 1 (the line is still 0 before a
// burst's first beat). The captured data is simply wrong; it counts in no error.
//
// Write leveling (MR2 OP7 = 1): on each DQS_t rising edge a lane samples CK_t and drives the
// sample on all its DQ TWLO_NCK tCK later; DQ is driven for as long as the mode is on.
//
// Reads, MRR and Read DQ Calibration: DQS_t is driven low for a 2 tCK static preamble ending
// RL x tCK + DQSCK_CLKS after the CAS-2 edge, then toggles 16 times half a tCK apart with DQ
// edge-aligned (DQ lags DQS by DQ_SKEW_CLKS clocks), then half a tCK of postamble. A burst that
// starts as the previous one ends follows it with no preamble. Up to four reads may be in
// flight. Read DQ Calibration returns, per beat, a bit of MR32 (beats 0-7) or MR40 (beats 8-15)
// on every DQ, inverted per DQ by MR15 (DQ0-7) and MR20 (DQ8-15), both 0x55 after reset as JEDEC
// sets them. MRR returns the register on
// DQ[7:0].
//
// RL and WL come from MR2 (write latency set A or B). MR5..MR8 read back the generics.
//
// Storage: one 16-beat burst per (bank, column[9:4]), tagged per byte lane with the row that
// wrote it. A lane's burst counts as written once all 16 beats are captured. Reading a row
// other than the one stored counts in `aliased` (a limitation of the model, not a design error);
// reading a location never fully written counts in `unwritten` and returns 16'hDEAD on every
// beat.
//
// Bus contention: `dq_driven` and `dqs_driven` say, per byte lane, when the other side drives DQ
// and DQS. Any clock in which both sides drive the same lines, at the controller's pins or after
// the board delay, is an error (code 26).
//
// `errors` counts design errors; `err_code` and `err_cycle` record the first one:
//   1 CS high on a command's second cycle      2 ACT-2 without ACT-1
//   3 MRW-2 without MRW-1                       4 CAS-2 without WR/RD/MRR/MPC
//   5 RD/WR to a closed bank                    6 REF with a bank open
//   7 unknown command                           8 write DQS missed the tDQSS window
//  11 write DQS edges not half a tCK apart      13 tRCD
//  14 tRP                                       15 tRFCab
//  16 tMRW                                      17 WR-1/RD-1/MRR-1/MPC-1 not followed by CAS-2
//  18 MRW-1 not followed by MRW-2               19 ACT to an open bank
//  20 DQS_c not the complement of DQS_t         21 refresh overdue (9 tREFI owed at the MR4 rate)
//  22 CA/CS changed in the clock before CK rose 23 CA/CS changed in the clock after CK rose
//  24 write burst stopped early                 25 MPC opcode the model does not have
//  26 both sides drive DQ or DQS                27 tZQCAL (ZQ latch too early)
//  28 tZQLAT (command too soon after ZQ latch)  29 tRAS
//  30 tRRD                                      31 tFAW
//  32 tCCD                                      33 tWR (write recovery before PRE)
//  34 tRTP                                      35 tWTR
//  36 more than four reads or writes in flight  37 ACT-1 not followed by ACT-2
// Codes 9 (DQ changed in the clock of a write DQS edge), 10 (DQ changed in the clock after it)
// and 12 (DQ not driven at it) are DQ timing and count in `dq_viol` (see Writes).

// One byte lane of the write path at the DRAM: the board delay, write capture and checks, and
// the lane's storage. `err` is a design error code for this clock (0 none), `viol` a DQ timing
// violation.
pub entity Lpddr4WriteLane<
    const SKEW_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const DQ_SKEW_CLKS: nat = 0
> {
    in clk: clock
    in cyc: bit[32]
    in half_ck: bit[32]
    in tck32: bit[32]
    // the lane at the controller's pins
    in dq_in: bit[8]
    in dq_driven: bit
    in dqs_t_in: bit
    in dqs_c_in: bit
    in dqs_driven: bit
    // the reference is above (vref_hi) or below (vref_lo) the receivers' window (see VREF(DQ))
    in vref_hi: bit
    in vref_lo: bit
    // a write CAS: the window for its first DQS rise, and its line and row
    in push: bit
    in push_lo: bit[32]
    in push_hi: bit[32]
    in push_line: bit[9]
    in push_row: bit[17]
    // storage reads: two data addresses {bank, column[9:4], beat} and one tag line
    in rd_addr_a: bit[13]
    in rd_addr_b: bit[13]
    in tag_line: bit[9]
    out rd_a: bit[8]
    out rd_b: bit[8]
    // {0 (a DQ timing violation is in the stored bits instead), written, row}
    out tag_out: bit[19]
    // the lane at the DRAM, after the board delay
    out dqs_seen: bit
    out dq_drv_seen: bit
    out dqs_drv_seen: bit
    out q_full: bit
    out err: bit[8]
    out viol: bit
}

impl Lpddr4WriteLane {
    // board delay line: {dqs_driven, dqs_c, dqs_t, dq_driven, dq[7:0]}
    signal hist: [bit[12]; 16]
    signal mem: [bit[8]; 8192]
    signal tag: [bit[19]; 512]
    // writes in flight
    signal q_lo: [bit[32]; 4]
    signal q_hi: [bit[32]; 4]
    signal q_line: [bit[9]; 4]
    signal q_row: [bit[17]; 4]
    signal q_head: bit[2] = 0
    signal q_n: bit[3] = 0
    // capture: 0 idle, 1 waiting for the first rise, 2 in the burst, 3 the clock after the last
    // edge (its hold check)
    signal st: bit[2] = 0
    signal lo: bit[32] = 0
    signal hi: bit[32] = 0
    signal line: bit[9] = 0
    signal row: bit[17] = 0
    signal beat: bit[5] = 0
    signal last: bit[32] = 0
    signal hold: bit = 0
    signal hold_dq: bit[8] = 0
    // the beat taken in the last clock, stored once its hold is checked: where, its value, and
    // the bits that changed in its clock
    signal h_addr: bit[13] = 0
    signal h_val: bit[8] = 0
    signal h_sv: bit[8] = 0
    signal dq_prev: bit[8] = 0
    signal dqs_prev: bit = 0
    // the line levels of the burst's previous beat (0 before its first)
    signal pb: bit[8] = 0

    let sk: bit[4] = SKEW_CLKS
    let dqk: bit[4] = DQ_SKEW_CLKS
    let dk: bit[4] = sk + dqk
    let raw: bit[12] = {dqs_driven, dqs_c_in, dqs_t_in, dq_driven, dq_in}
    let hs: bit[12] = if sk == 0 { raw } else { hist[cyc[3:0] - sk] }
    let hd: bit[12] = if dk == 0 { raw } else { hist[cyc[3:0] - dk] }
    let dq: bit[8] = hd[7:0]
    let dq_drv: bit = hd[8]
    let dqs: bit = hs[9]
    let dqs_c: bit = hs[10]
    let dqs_drv: bit = hs[11]

    let dqs_edge: bit = if dqs != dqs_prev { 1 } else { 0 }
    let dqs_rise: bit = if dqs == 1 && dqs_prev == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let since_edge: bit[32] = cyc - last
    let first: bit = if st == 1 && dqs_rise == 1 && cyc >= lo { 1 } else { 0 }
    let take: bit = if first == 1 || (st == 2 && dqs_edge == 1) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let setup_v: bit = if take == 1 && (dq != dq_prev || dq_drv == 0) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let hold_v: bit = if hold == 1 && dq != hold_dq { 1 } else { 0 }
    // the DQ bits taken in violation: those that changed in the clock of the edge (all when DQ is
    // not driven) and those that change in the clock after it
    let sv_bits: bit[8] = if dq_drv == 0 { 8'hFF } else { dq ^ dq_prev }
    let hv_bits: bit[8] = if hold == 1 { dq ^ hold_dq } else { 8'h00 }
    let err_now: bit[8] =
        if st == 1 && cyc > hi { 8 }
        else { if st == 2 && dqs_edge == 1 && (since_edge + 1 < half_ck || since_edge > half_ck + 1) { 11 }
        else { if take == 1 && dqs_c == dqs { 20 }
        else { if st == 2 && since_edge > tck32 { 24 }
        else { 0 } } } }
    let idx: bit[4] = if st == 1 { 4'h0 } else { beat[3:0] }
    // what the receivers take with the reference outside their window
    let dq_v: bit[8] = if vref_hi == 1 { dq & pb } else { if vref_lo == 1 { dq | pb } else { dq } }
    let q_tail: bit[2] = q_head + q_n[1:0]
    let push_ok: bit = if push == 1 && q_n != 4 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let load: bit = if (st == 0 || st == 3) && q_n != 0 { 1 } else { 0 }

    on(clk.rise) {
        hist[cyc[3:0]] = raw
        dq_prev = dq
        dqs_prev = dqs
        hold = take
        hold_dq = dq
        // a beat is stored the clock after it is taken (edges are at least two clocks apart),
        // with the bits taken in violation inverted
        if hold == 1 {
            mem[h_addr] = h_val ^ h_sv ^ hv_bits
        }
        if take == 1 {
            h_addr = {line, idx}
            h_val = dq_v
            h_sv = sv_bits
            pb = dq
        }
        if push_ok == 1 {
            q_lo[q_tail] = push_lo
            q_hi[q_tail] = push_hi
            q_line[q_tail] = push_line
            q_row[q_tail] = push_row
        }
        q_n = if push_ok == 1 && load == 0 { q_n + 1 } else { if push_ok == 0 && load == 1 { q_n - 1 } else { q_n } }

        if st == 1 {
            if cyc > hi {
                st = 0
            } else {
                if first == 1 {
                    beat = 1
                    last = cyc
                    st = 2
                }
            }
        }
        if st == 2 {
            if since_edge > tck32 {
                st = 0
            } else {
                if dqs_edge == 1 {
                    last = cyc
                    beat = beat + 1
                    if beat == 15 { st = 3 }
                }
            }
        }
        if st == 3 {
            // the burst counts as written only once all 16 beats are in and held (a violation
            // is in the stored bits, so nothing reads back inverted as a whole)
            tag[line] = {1'b0, 1'b1, row}
            st = 0
        }
        if load == 1 {
            st = 1
            lo = q_lo[q_head]
            hi = q_hi[q_head]
            line = q_line[q_head]
            row = q_row[q_head]
            q_head = q_head + 1
            pb = 0
        }
    }

    rd_a = mem[rd_addr_a]
    rd_b = mem[rd_addr_b]
    tag_out = tag[tag_line]
    dqs_seen = dqs
    dq_drv_seen = dq_drv
    dqs_drv_seen = dqs_drv
    q_full = if q_n == 4 { 1 } else { 0 }
    err = err_now
    viol = if setup_v == 1 || hold_v == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
}

pub entity Lpddr4ChannelModel<
    const MR5: nat = 255,
    const MR6: nat = 0,
    const MR7: nat = 0,
    const MR8: nat = 16,
    const DQSCK_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const DQ_SKEW_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const TRCD_NCK: nat = 4,
    const TRP_NCK: nat = 4,
    const TRAS_NCK: nat = 3,
    const TRRD_NCK: nat = 4,
    const TFAW_NCK: nat = 8,
    const TRFC_NCK: nat = 3,
    const TMRW_NCK: nat = 10,
    const TREFI_NCK: nat = 48,
    const TWR_NCK: nat = 4,
    const TWTR_NCK: nat = 8,
    const TRTP_NCK: nat = 8,
    const TCCD_NCK: nat = 8,
    const TZQCAL_NCK: nat = 16,
    const TZQLAT_NCK: nat = 8,
    const WR_SKEW0_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const WR_SKEW1_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const WR_DQ_SKEW0_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const WR_DQ_SKEW1_CLKS: nat = 0,
    const TWLO_NCK: nat = 8,
    // the MR14 levels (see VREF(DQ)) the write receivers work at
    const VREF_OK_LO: nat = 0,
    const VREF_OK_HI: nat = 255,
    // MR4 (refresh rate, OP[2:0]) the device reports: MR4_COLD, then MR4_HOT from clock
    // MR4_HOT_AT_NCK (0 = never). 3 = 1x tREFI, 4 = 0.5x, 5 and up = 0.25x (6 and 7 derate AC
    // timings too, which this model does not check); refresh is checked against the current rate
    const MR4_COLD: nat = 3,
    const MR4_HOT: nat = 3,
    const MR4_HOT_AT_NCK: nat = 0
> {
    in clk: clock
    in reset_n: bit
    in ck_t: bit
    in cke: bit
    in cs: bit
    in ca: bit[6]
    in dq_in: bit[16]
    // per byte lane: what the controller side drives
    in dq_driven: bit[2]
    in dqs_t_in: bit[2]
    in dqs_c_in: bit[2]
    in dqs_driven: bit[2]
    out dq_out: bit[16]
    out dq_oe: bit
    out dqs_out: bit
    out dqs_oe: bit
    out errors: bit[16]
    out err_code: bit[8]
    out err_cycle: bit[32]
    out contention: bit[16]
    out dq_viol: bit[16]
    out aliased: bit[16]
    out unwritten: bit[16]
    out n_act: bit[32]
    out n_wr: bit[32]
    out n_rd: bit[32]
    out n_mrw: bit[16]
    out n_mrr: bit[16]
    out n_ref: bit[32]
    // refreshes owed at the current MR4 rate (error 21 past 8)
    out ref_owed: bit[8]
    out n_zq: bit[16]
    out t_ck_clks: bit[8]
    out mr2_o: bit[8]
    out mr13_o: bit[8]
}

impl Lpddr4ChannelModel {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------ state
    signal cyc: bit[32] = 0
    signal nck: bit[32] = 0
    signal ck_prev: bit = 0
    signal last_rise: bit[32] = 0
    signal t_ck: bit[8] = 8
    signal ca_prev: bit[6] = 0
    signal cs_prev: bit = 0
    signal hold_chk: bit = 0
    signal hold_ca: bit[6] = 0
    signal hold_cs: bit = 0
    signal have_first: bit = 0
    signal first: bit[6] = 0
    // 0 none, 1 WR-1, 2 RD-1, 3 MRW-1, 4 MRR-1, 5 ACT-1, 6 MPC-1 Read DQ Calibration
    signal pending: bit[3] = 0
    signal p_bank: bit[3] = 0
    signal p_c9: bit = 0
    signal p_ma: bit[6] = 0
    signal p_op7: bit = 0
    signal p_row: bit[17] = 0
    signal mr1: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr2: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr3: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr11: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr12: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr13: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr14: bit[8] = 0
    signal mr22: bit[8] = 0
    // Read DQ Calibration: invert masks (MR15 DQ0-7, MR20 DQ8-15) and patterns (MR32, MR40),
    // JEDEC defaults
    // JEDEC defaults: DQ0, 2, 4, 6 (and 8, 10, 12, 14) inverted
    signal mr15: bit[8] = 8'h55
    signal mr20: bit[8] = 8'h55
    signal mr32: bit[8] = 8'h5A
    signal mr40: bit[8] = 8'h3C
    signal last_mrw: bit[32] = 0
    signal any_mrw: bit = 0
    signal open_valid: bit[8] = 0
    signal open_row: [bit[17]; 8]
    signal act_at: [bit[32]; 8]
    signal pre_at: [bit[32]; 8]
    signal wr_end_at: [bit[32]; 8]
    signal rd_cas_at: [bit[32]; 8]
    signal wr_seen: bit[8] = 0
    signal rd_seen: bit[8] = 0
    signal wr_end_any: bit[32] = 0
    signal wr_any: bit = 0
    signal rd_cas_any: bit[32] = 0
    signal rd_any: bit = 0
    signal last_cas: bit[32] = 0
    signal cas_seen: bit = 0
    // the last four ACTs (h0 newest), for tRRD and tFAW
    signal act_h0: bit[32] = 0
    signal act_h1: bit[32] = 0
    signal act_h2: bit[32] = 0
    signal act_h3: bit[32] = 0
    signal act_cnt: bit[3] = 0
    signal ref_at: bit[32] = 0
    signal ref_seen: bit = 0
    // refresh owed: one per tREFI (at the MR4 rate) since the first REF, less one per REF
    signal ref_acc: bit[32] = 0
    signal ref_debt: bit[8] = 0
    signal zq_start_at: bit[32] = 0
    signal zq_started: bit = 0
    signal zq_lat_at: bit[32] = 0
    signal zq_latched: bit = 0
    signal errors_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal err_code_r: bit[8] = 0
    signal err_cycle_r: bit[32] = 0
    signal cont_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal aliased_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal unwritten_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal n_act_r: bit[32] = 0
    signal n_wr_r: bit[32] = 0
    signal n_rd_r: bit[32] = 0
    signal n_mrw_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal n_mrr_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal n_ref_r: bit[32] = 0
    signal n_zq_r: bit[16] = 0
    // write leveling feedback per lane: pending, due clock, sampled CK, value driven
    signal fb_pend: bit[2] = 0
    signal fb_at0: bit[32] = 0
    signal fb_at1: bit[32] = 0
    signal fb_s: bit[2] = 0
    signal fb_v: bit[2] = 0
    signal wl_prev: bit[2] = 0
    signal viol_r: bit[16] = 0
    // reads in flight: clock of the first data DQS rise, line, kind (0 data, 1 MRR, 2 Read DQ
    // Calibration), whether the stored row matches, and the MRR value
    signal rq_t0: [bit[32]; 4]
    signal rq_line: [bit[9]; 4]
    signal rq_kind: [bit[2]; 4]
    // per lane: stored row matches, and the lane's data reads back inverted
    signal rq_ok0: bit[4] = 0
    signal rq_ok1: bit[4] = 0
    signal rq_cor0: bit[4] = 0
    signal rq_cor1: bit[4] = 0
    signal rq_mrv: [bit[8]; 4]
    signal rq_head: bit[2] = 0
    signal rq_n: bit[3] = 0
    // read drive: 0 idle, 1 preamble, 2 burst, 3 postamble
    signal rd_st: bit[2] = 0
    signal rd_sub: bit[8] = 0
    signal rd_b: bit[5] = 0
    signal rd_line: bit[9] = 0
    signal rd_kind: bit[2] = 0
    signal rd_ok0: bit = 0
    signal rd_ok1: bit = 0
    signal rd_cor0: bit = 0
    signal rd_cor1: bit = 0
    signal rd_mrv: bit[8] = 0
    signal dq_out_r: bit[16] = 0
    signal dq_oe_r: bit = 0
    signal dqs_out_r: bit = 0
    signal dqs_oe_r: bit = 0
    // DQ_SKEW_CLKS delay line for the read DQ drive
    signal skew_dq: [bit[16]; 8]
    signal skew_oe: bit[8] = 0

    // ------------------------------------------------------------ latencies and timing
    let rl: bit[8] = match mr2[2:0] {
        0 => 6,
        1 => 10,
        2 => 14,
        3 => 20,
        4 => 24,
        5 => 28,
        6 => 32,
        _ => 36
    }
    let wl_a: bit[8] = match mr2[5:3] {
        0 => 4,
        1 => 6,
        2 => 8,
        3 => 10,
        4 => 12,
        5 => 14,
        6 => 16,
        _ => 18
    }
    let wl_b: bit[8] = match mr2[5:3] {
        0 => 4,
        1 => 8,
        2 => 12,
        3 => 18,
        4 => 22,
        5 => 26,
        6 => 30,
        _ => 34
    }
    let wl: bit[8] = if mr2[6] == 1 { wl_b } else { wl_a }
    let tck32: bit[32] = {24'h000000, t_ck}
    let half_ck: bit[32] = tck32 >> 1
    let quarter_ck: bit[32] = tck32 >> 2
    let wl_clks: bit[32] = {24'h000000, wl} * tck32
    let rl_clks: bit[32] = {24'h000000, rl} * tck32
    let dqsck32: bit[32] = DQSCK_CLKS
    let skew3: bit[3] = DQ_SKEW_CLKS
    // CK cycle (second-cycle edge numbering) at which a write burst ends: WL + BL/2 + 1
    let wl32: bit[32] = {24'h000000, wl}

    let ck_rise: bit = if ck_t == 1 && ck_prev == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let dev_on: bit = if reset_n == 1 && cke == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rise_gap: bit[32] = cyc - last_rise

    // second-cycle decode helpers (valid when have_first == 1 and cs == 0 on a rise)
    let a: bit[6] = first
    let b: bit[6] = ca
    let is_first: bit = if ck_rise == 1 && dev_on == 1 && cs == 1 && have_first == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_cmd: bit = if ck_rise == 1 && dev_on == 1 && cs == 0 && have_first == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_act1: bit = if is_cmd == 1 && a[1:0] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_act2: bit = if is_cmd == 1 && a[1:0] == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let op5: bit[5] = a[4:0]
    let is_other: bit = if is_cmd == 1 && a[0] == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_mpc: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    // MPC opcodes (OP6 = first cycle CA5, OP5:0 = second cycle): 0x43 Read DQ Calibration,
    // 0x4B/0x4D DQS oscillator start/stop, 0x4F/0x51 ZQ calibration start/latch. The FIFO
    // opcodes (0x41, 0x47) are not modelled.
    let mpc_rdc: bit = if is_mpc == 1 && a[5] == 1 && b == 3 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let mpc_zqs: bit = if is_mpc == 1 && a[5] == 1 && b == 15 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let mpc_zql: bit = if is_mpc == 1 && a[5] == 1 && b == 17 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let mpc_known: bit = if is_mpc == 1 && (a[5] == 0 || b == 3 || b == 11 || b == 13 || b == 15 || b == 17) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_pre: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 16 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_ref: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 8 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_wr1: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 4 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_rd1: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 2 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_mrw1: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 6 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_mrw2: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 22 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_mrr1: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 14 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_cas2: bit = if is_other == 1 && op5 == 18 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let is_unknown: bit = if is_other == 1 && is_mpc == 0 && is_pre == 0 && is_ref == 0 && is_wr1 == 0 && is_rd1 == 0 && is_mrw1 == 0 && is_mrw2 == 0 && is_mrr1 == 0 && is_cas2 == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }

    let ba: bit[3] = b[2:0]
    let pre_all: bit = a[5]
    let ba_open: bit = open_valid[ba]
    let act_bank: bit[3] = p_bank
    let since_act: bit[32] = nck - act_at[ba]
    let since_pre: bit[32] = nck - pre_at[ba]
    let since_ref: bit[32] = nck - ref_at
    let since_mrw: bit[32] = nck - last_mrw
    let cas_bank: bit[3] = p_bank
    let cas_col: bit[10] = {p_c9, a[5], b, 2'b00}
    let cas_line: bit[9] = {cas_bank, cas_col[9:4]}
    let cas_row: bit[17] = open_row[cas_bank]
    let cas_open: bit = open_valid[cas_bank]
    let tag0: bit[19] = lane0.tag_out
    let tag1: bit[19] = lane1.tag_out
    let cas_wr0: bit = tag0[17]
    let cas_wr1: bit = tag1[17]
    let cas_hit0: bit = if tag0[17] == 1 && tag0[16:0] == cas_row { 1 } else { 0 }
    let cas_hit1: bit = if tag1[17] == 1 && tag1[16:0] == cas_row { 1 } else { 0 }
    let cas_alias: bit = if (tag0[17] == 1 && tag0[16:0] != cas_row) || (tag1[17] == 1 && tag1[16:0] != cas_row) { 1 } else { 0 }
    // (generics read through lets: a generic used directly in a match arm is not substituted)
    let mr5_c: bit[8] = MR5
    let mr6_c: bit[8] = MR6
    let mr7_c: bit[8] = MR7
    let mr8_c: bit[8] = MR8
    let mr4_cold_c: bit[8] = MR4_COLD
    let mr4_hot_c: bit[8] = MR4_HOT
    let mr4_hot_at: bit[32] = MR4_HOT_AT_NCK
    let mr4_now: bit[8] = if mr4_hot_at != 0 && nck >= mr4_hot_at { mr4_hot_c } else { mr4_cold_c }
    let ref_sh: bit[32] = if mr4_now[2:0] == 4 { 1 } else { if mr4_now[2:0] >= 5 { 2 } else { 0 } }
    let trefi32: bit[32] = TREFI_NCK
    let refi_req: bit[32] = trefi32 >> ref_sh
    let ref_tick: bit = if ck_rise == 1 && ref_seen == 1 && ref_acc + 1 >= refi_req { 1 } else { 0 }
    let mr_read: bit[8] = match p_ma {
        1 => mr1,
        2 => mr2,
        3 => mr3,
        4 => mr4_now,
        5 => mr5_c,
        6 => mr6_c,
        7 => mr7_c,
        8 => mr8_c,
        11 => mr11,
        12 => mr12,
        13 => mr13,
        14 => mr14,
        15 => mr15,
        20 => mr20,
        22 => mr22,
        32 => mr32,
        40 => mr40,
        _ => 0
    }
    let new_act_row: bit[17] = p_row | {7'b0000000, a[5:2], b[5:0]}

    // ---------------------------------------------------------------- timing checks
    // tRAS: a precharge of an open bank too soon after its ACT (all banks for PREab)
    let ras_b0: bit = if open_valid[0] == 1 && nck - act_at[0] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b1: bit = if open_valid[1] == 1 && nck - act_at[1] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b2: bit = if open_valid[2] == 1 && nck - act_at[2] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b3: bit = if open_valid[3] == 1 && nck - act_at[3] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b4: bit = if open_valid[4] == 1 && nck - act_at[4] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b5: bit = if open_valid[5] == 1 && nck - act_at[5] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b6: bit = if open_valid[6] == 1 && nck - act_at[6] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_b7: bit = if open_valid[7] == 1 && nck - act_at[7] < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_any: bit = ras_b0 | ras_b1 | ras_b2 | ras_b3 | ras_b4 | ras_b5 | ras_b6 | ras_b7
    let ras_one: bit = if ba_open == 1 && since_act < TRAS_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ras_err: bit = if is_pre == 1 && ((pre_all == 1 && ras_any == 1) || (pre_all == 0 && ras_one == 1)) { 1 } else { 0 }
    // tWR: write recovery, from the end of the bank's last write burst to its precharge
    let wr_one: bit = if wr_seen[ba] == 1 && nck < wr_end_at[ba] + TWR_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wr_all: bit = if wr_any == 1 && nck < wr_end_any + TWR_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let twr_err: bit = if is_pre == 1 && ((pre_all == 1 && wr_all == 1) || (pre_all == 0 && wr_one == 1)) { 1 } else { 0 }
    // tRTP: read CAS to precharge (BL16: BL/2 + max(8, tRTP) - 8 = tRTP)
    let rtp_one: bit = if rd_seen[ba] == 1 && nck - rd_cas_at[ba] < TRTP_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rtp_all: bit = if rd_any == 1 && nck - rd_cas_any < TRTP_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rtp_err: bit = if is_pre == 1 && ((pre_all == 1 && rtp_all == 1) || (pre_all == 0 && rtp_one == 1)) { 1 } else { 0 }
    // tRRD and tFAW, measured between ACT-2 edges
    let rrd_err: bit = if is_act2 == 1 && act_cnt != 0 && nck - act_h0 < TRRD_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let faw_err: bit = if is_act2 == 1 && act_cnt == 4 && nck - act_h3 < TFAW_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    // tCCD between CAS-2 commands; tWTR from the end of a write burst to a read CAS
    let ccd_err: bit = if is_cas2 == 1 && cas_seen == 1 && nck - last_cas < TCCD_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wtr_err: bit = if is_cas2 == 1 && (pending == 2 || pending == 4 || pending == 6) && wr_any == 1 && nck < wr_end_any + TWTR_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }
    // ZQ calibration: latch no sooner than tZQCAL after start; nothing within tZQLAT of latch
    let zqcal_err: bit = if mpc_zql == 1 && (zq_started == 0 || nck - zq_start_at < TZQCAL_NCK) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let zqlat_err: bit = if is_first == 1 && zq_latched == 1 && nck - zq_lat_at < TZQLAT_NCK { 1 } else { 0 }

    // errors found this clock, as one code (the lowest-listed wins if several)
    let cmd_err: bit[8] =
        if ck_rise == 1 && dev_on == 1 && cs == 1 && have_first == 1 { 1 }
        else { if ck_rise == 1 && dev_on == 1 && (ca != ca_prev || cs != cs_prev) { 22 }
        else { if is_act2 == 1 && pending != 5 { 2 }
        else { if is_mrw2 == 1 && pending != 3 { 3 }
        else { if is_cas2 == 1 && pending != 1 && pending != 2 && pending != 4 && pending != 6 { 4 }
        else { if is_cas2 == 1 && (pending == 1 || pending == 2) && cas_open == 0 { 5 }
        else { if is_ref == 1 && open_valid != 0 { 6 }
        else { if is_unknown == 1 { 7 }
        else { if is_mpc == 1 && mpc_known == 0 { 25 }
        else { if is_cmd == 1 && is_cas2 == 0 && (pending == 1 || pending == 2 || pending == 4 || pending == 6) { 17 }
        else { if is_cmd == 1 && is_mrw2 == 0 && pending == 3 { 18 }
        else { if is_cmd == 1 && is_act2 == 0 && pending == 5 { 37 }
        else { if (is_wr1 == 1 || is_rd1 == 1) && ba_open == 1 && since_act < TRCD_NCK { 13 }
        else { if is_act1 == 1 && ba_open == 1 { 19 }
        else { if is_act1 == 1 && since_pre < TRP_NCK { 14 }
        else { if is_act1 == 1 && since_ref < TRFC_NCK && ref_seen == 1 { 15 }
        else { if is_first == 1 && any_mrw == 1 && since_mrw < TMRW_NCK { 16 }
        else { if zqcal_err == 1 { 27 }
        else { if zqlat_err == 1 { 28 }
        else { if ras_err == 1 { 29 }
        else { if rrd_err == 1 { 30 }
        else { if faw_err == 1 { 31 }
        else { if ccd_err == 1 { 32 }
        else { if twr_err == 1 { 33 }
        else { if rtp_err == 1 { 34 }
        else { if wtr_err == 1 { 35 }
        else { 0 } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } } }
    // DQ as driven, after the DQ_SKEW_CLKS delay
    let skew_at: bit[3] = cyc[2:0] - skew3
    let dq_skewed: bit[16] = if skew3 == 0 { dq_out_r } else { skew_dq[skew_at] }
    let oe_skewed: bit = if skew3 == 0 { dq_oe_r } else { skew_oe[skew_at] }
    let hold_err: bit[8] = if hold_chk == 1 && (ca != hold_ca || cs != hold_cs) { 23 } else { 0 }
    // more than 8 refreshes postponed (JEDEC): the ninth tREFI with nothing refreshed
    let ref_err: bit[8] = if ref_tick == 1 && ref_debt >= 9 && is_ref == 0 { 21 } else { 0 }
    // write leveling: MR2 OP7; DQ carries each lane's CK sample
    let wl_mode: bit = mr2[7]
    let twlo32: bit[32] = TWLO_NCK
    let twlo_clks: bit[32] = twlo32 * tck32
    let wl_rise0: bit = if wl_mode == 1 && lane0.dqs_seen == 1 && wl_prev[0] == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wl_rise1: bit = if wl_mode == 1 && lane1.dqs_seen == 1 && wl_prev[1] == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let dram_dq_oe: bit = if oe_skewed == 1 || wl_mode == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    // the controller side drives a lane at its pins or, after the board delay, at the DRAM
    let ctl_dq: bit = if dq_driven != 0 || lane0.dq_drv_seen == 1 || lane1.dq_drv_seen == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let ctl_dqs: bit = if dqs_driven != 0 || lane0.dqs_drv_seen == 1 || lane1.dqs_drv_seen == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let both_drive: bit = if (dram_dq_oe == 1 && ctl_dq == 1) || (dqs_oe_r == 1 && ctl_dqs == 1) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let cont_err: bit[8] = if both_drive == 1 { 26 } else { 0 }
    let wq_full: bit = if lane0.q_full == 1 || lane1.q_full == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rq_full: bit = if rq_n == 4 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wr_cas: bit = if is_cas2 == 1 && pending == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rd_cas: bit = if is_cas2 == 1 && (pending == 2 || pending == 4 || pending == 6) { 1 } else { 0 }
    let q_err: bit[8] = if (wr_cas == 1 && wq_full == 1) || (rd_cas == 1 && rq_full == 1) { 36 } else { 0 }

    // write capture checks, per lane
    let wr_err: bit[8] = if lane0.err != 0 { lane0.err } else { lane1.err }
    let err_now: bit[8] =
        if cmd_err != 0 { cmd_err }
        else { if hold_err != 0 { hold_err }
        else { if ref_err != 0 { ref_err }
        else { if cont_err != 0 { cont_err }
        else { if q_err != 0 { q_err }
        else { wr_err } } } } }

    // a write CAS for the lanes' queues: the window for the first data DQS rise
    let wr_push: bit = if is_cas2 == 1 && pending == 1 && wq_full == 0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let wr_lo: bit[32] = cyc + wl_clks + half_ck + quarter_ck
    let wr_hi: bit[32] = cyc + wl_clks + tck32 + quarter_ck
    let rq_tail: bit[2] = rq_head + rq_n[1:0]

    // read data for the current beat
    let rd_b4: bit[4] = rd_b[3:0]
    let rd_b4_next: bit[4] = rd_b4 + 1
    let rd_addr_next: bit[13] = {rd_line, rd_b4_next}
    let rdc_bit_next: bit = if rd_b4_next[3] == 0 { mr32[rd_b4_next[2:0]] } else { mr40[rd_b4_next[2:0]] }
    let rdc_mask: bit[16] = {mr20, mr15}
    let rdc_word_next: bit[16] = if rdc_bit_next == 1 { ~rdc_mask } else { rdc_mask }
    let rd_byte0: bit[8] = if rd_ok0 == 0 { 8'hAD } else { if rd_cor0 == 1 { ~lane0.rd_a } else { lane0.rd_a } }
    let rd_byte1: bit[8] = if rd_ok1 == 0 { 8'hDE } else { if rd_cor1 == 1 { ~lane1.rd_a } else { lane1.rd_a } }
    let rd_word_next: bit[16] = {rd_byte1, rd_byte0}
    let rd_data_next: bit[16] = if rd_kind == 2 { rdc_word_next } else { if rd_kind == 1 { {8'h00, rd_mrv} } else { rd_word_next } }
    // the head of the read queue, for starting its burst (beat 0)
    let h_line: bit[9] = rq_line[rq_head]
    let h_kind: bit[2] = rq_kind[rq_head]
    let h_ok0: bit = rq_ok0[rq_head]
    let h_ok1: bit = rq_ok1[rq_head]
    let h_cor0: bit = rq_cor0[rq_head]
    let h_cor1: bit = rq_cor1[rq_head]
    let h_mrv: bit[8] = rq_mrv[rq_head]
    let h_t0: bit[32] = rq_t0[rq_head]
    let h_rdc_bit: bit = mr32[0]
    let h_rdc_word: bit[16] = if h_rdc_bit == 1 { ~rdc_mask } else { rdc_mask }
    let h_byte0: bit[8] = if h_ok0 == 0 { 8'hAD } else { if h_cor0 == 1 { ~lane0.rd_b } else { lane0.rd_b } }
    let h_byte1: bit[8] = if h_ok1 == 0 { 8'hDE } else { if h_cor1 == 1 { ~lane1.rd_b } else { lane1.rd_b } }
    let h_word: bit[16] = {h_byte1, h_byte0}
    let h_data: bit[16] = if h_kind == 2 { h_rdc_word } else { if h_kind == 1 { {8'h00, h_mrv} } else { h_word } }
    let rq_due: bit = if rq_n != 0 && cyc + 1 == h_t0 { 1 } else { 0 }
    let rq_pre_due: bit = if rq_n != 0 && cyc + 1 + tck32 + tck32 >= h_t0 { 1 } else { 0 }

    // VREF(DQ) level and whether it is in the receivers' window
    let vref_ok_lo: bit[8] = VREF_OK_LO
    let vref_ok_hi: bit[8] = VREF_OK_HI
    let vref_lvl: bit[8] = if mr14[6] == 1 { 8'd55 + {2'b00, mr14[5:0]} } else { 8'd25 + {2'b00, mr14[5:0]} }
    let vref_hi: bit = if vref_lvl > vref_ok_hi { 1 } else { 0 }
    let vref_lo: bit = if vref_lvl < vref_ok_lo { 1 } else { 0 }

    inst lane0 = Lpddr4WriteLane<WR_SKEW0_CLKS, WR_DQ_SKEW0_CLKS> {
        clk: clk,
        cyc: cyc,
        half_ck: half_ck,
        tck32: tck32,
        dq_in: dq_in[7:0],
        dq_driven: dq_driven[0],
        dqs_t_in: dqs_t_in[0],
        dqs_c_in: dqs_c_in[0],
        dqs_driven: dqs_driven[0],
        vref_hi: vref_hi,
        vref_lo: vref_lo,
        push: wr_push,
        push_lo: wr_lo,
        push_hi: wr_hi,
        push_line: cas_line,
        push_row: cas_row,
        rd_addr_a: rd_addr_next,
        rd_addr_b: {h_line, 4'h0},
        tag_line: cas_line
    }
    inst lane1 = Lpddr4WriteLane<WR_SKEW1_CLKS, WR_DQ_SKEW1_CLKS> {
        clk: clk,
        cyc: cyc,
        half_ck: half_ck,
        tck32: tck32,
        dq_in: dq_in[15:8],
        dq_driven: dq_driven[1],
        dqs_t_in: dqs_t_in[1],
        dqs_c_in: dqs_c_in[1],
        dqs_driven: dqs_driven[1],
        vref_hi: vref_hi,
        vref_lo: vref_lo,
        push: wr_push,
        push_lo: wr_lo,
        push_hi: wr_hi,
        push_line: cas_line,
        push_row: cas_row,
        rd_addr_a: rd_addr_next,
        rd_addr_b: {h_line, 4'h0},
        tag_line: cas_line
    }

    on(clk.rise) {
        cyc = cyc + 1
        ck_prev = ck_t
        ca_prev = ca
        cs_prev = cs
        wl_prev = {lane1.dqs_seen, lane0.dqs_seen}
        skew_dq[cyc[2:0]] = dq_out_r
        skew_oe[cyc[2:0]] = dq_oe_r

        if err_now != 0 {
            errors_r = if errors_r == 65535 { 65535 } else { errors_r + 1 }
            if errors_r == 0 {
                err_code_r = err_now
                err_cycle_r = cyc
            }
        }
        if both_drive == 1 {
            cont_r = if cont_r == 65535 { 65535 } else { cont_r + 1 }
        }
        if lane0.viol == 1 || lane1.viol == 1 {
            viol_r = if viol_r == 65535 { 65535 } else { viol_r + 1 }
        }

        // write leveling: a lane's DQS rise samples CK; the sample is driven tWLO later
        if wl_rise0 == 1 {
            fb_pend[0] = 1
            fb_at0 = cyc + twlo_clks
            fb_s[0] = ck_t
        } else {
            if fb_pend[0] == 1 && cyc >= fb_at0 {
                fb_pend[0] = 0
                fb_v[0] = fb_s[0]
            }
        }
        if wl_rise1 == 1 {
            fb_pend[1] = 1
            fb_at1 = cyc + twlo_clks
            fb_s[1] = ck_t
        } else {
            if fb_pend[1] == 1 && cyc >= fb_at1 {
                fb_pend[1] = 0
                fb_v[1] = fb_s[1]
            }
        }
        if wl_mode == 0 {
            fb_pend = 0
            fb_v = 0
        }

        // CA/CS hold: checked on the clock after each CK rise
        hold_chk = if ck_rise == 1 && dev_on == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
        hold_ca = ca
        hold_cs = cs

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------- commands
        if ck_rise == 1 {
            nck = nck + 1
            if ref_tick == 1 { ref_acc = 0 } else { if ref_seen == 1 { ref_acc = ref_acc + 1 } }
            ref_debt = if ref_tick == 1 && is_ref == 0 { if ref_debt == 255 { 255 } else { ref_debt + 1 } } else { if ref_tick == 0 && is_ref == 1 && ref_debt != 0 { ref_debt - 1 } else { ref_debt } }
            if last_rise != 0 { t_ck = rise_gap[7:0] }
            last_rise = cyc
            if dev_on == 0 {
                have_first = 0
            } else {
                if cs == 1 {
                    have_first = 1
                    first = ca
                } else {
                    if have_first == 1 {
                        have_first = 0
                        if is_act1 == 1 {
                            p_row = {b[3], a[5:2], b[5:4], 10'b0000000000}
                            p_bank = b[2:0]
                            pending = 5
                        }
                        if is_act2 == 1 {
                            open_row[act_bank] = new_act_row
                            open_valid[act_bank] = 1
                            act_at[act_bank] = nck
                            act_h0 = nck
                            act_h1 = act_h0
                            act_h2 = act_h1
                            act_h3 = act_h2
                            act_cnt = if act_cnt == 4 { 4 } else { act_cnt + 1 }
                            n_act_r = n_act_r + 1
                            pending = 0
                        }
                        if is_pre == 1 {
                            if pre_all == 1 {
                                open_valid = 0
                                pre_at[0] = nck
                                pre_at[1] = nck
                                pre_at[2] = nck
                                pre_at[3] = nck
                                pre_at[4] = nck
                                pre_at[5] = nck
                                pre_at[6] = nck
                                pre_at[7] = nck
                            } else {
                                open_valid[ba] = 0
                                pre_at[ba] = nck
                            }
                            pending = 0
                        }
                        if is_ref == 1 {
                            ref_at = nck
                            ref_seen = 1
                            n_ref_r = n_ref_r + 1
                            pending = 0
                        }
                        if is_mpc == 1 {
                            pending = if mpc_rdc == 1 { 6 } else { 0 }
                            if mpc_zqs == 1 {
                                zq_start_at = nck
                                zq_started = 1
                            }
                            if mpc_zql == 1 {
                                zq_lat_at = nck
                                zq_latched = 1
                                zq_started = 0
                                n_zq_r = n_zq_r + 1
                            }
                        }
                        if is_wr1 == 1 {
                            pending = 1
                            p_bank = b[2:0]
                            p_c9 = b[4]
                        }
                        if is_rd1 == 1 {
                            pending = 2
                            p_bank = b[2:0]
                            p_c9 = b[4]
                        }
                        if is_mrw1 == 1 {
                            pending = 3
                            p_ma = b
                            p_op7 = a[5]
                        }
                        if is_mrr1 == 1 {
                            pending = 4
                            p_ma = b
                        }
                        if is_mrw2 == 1 {
                            match p_ma {
                                1 => { mr1 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                2 => { mr2 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                3 => { mr3 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                11 => { mr11 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                12 => { mr12 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                13 => { mr13 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                14 => { mr14 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                15 => { mr15 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                20 => { mr20 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                22 => { mr22 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                32 => { mr32 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                40 => { mr40 = {p_op7, a[5], b} },
                                _ => {}
                            }
                            last_mrw = nck
                            any_mrw = 1
                            n_mrw_r = n_mrw_r + 1
                            pending = 0
                        }
                        if is_cas2 == 1 {
                            last_cas = nck
                            cas_seen = 1
                            if pending == 1 && wq_full == 0 {
                                wr_end_at[cas_bank] = nck + wl32 + 9
                                wr_seen[cas_bank] = 1
                                wr_end_any = nck + wl32 + 9
                                wr_any = 1
                                n_wr_r = n_wr_r + 1
                                if cas_alias == 1 {
                                    aliased_r = aliased_r + 1
                                }
                            }
                            if (pending == 2 || pending == 4 || pending == 6) && rq_full == 0 {
                                rq_t0[rq_tail] = cyc + rl_clks + dqsck32
                                rq_line[rq_tail] = cas_line
                                rq_kind[rq_tail] = if pending == 4 { 1 } else { if pending == 6 { 2 } else { 0 } }
                                rq_ok0[rq_tail] = cas_hit0
                                rq_ok1[rq_tail] = cas_hit1
                                rq_cor0[rq_tail] = tag0[18]
                                rq_cor1[rq_tail] = tag1[18]
                                rq_mrv[rq_tail] = mr_read
                                rq_n = rq_n + 1
                                if pending == 2 {
                                    rd_cas_at[cas_bank] = nck
                                    rd_seen[cas_bank] = 1
                                    rd_cas_any = nck
                                    rd_any = 1
                                }
                                if pending == 6 { n_rd_r = n_rd_r + 1 }
                                if pending == 2 {
                                    n_rd_r = n_rd_r + 1
                                    if cas_wr0 == 0 || cas_wr1 == 0 { unwritten_r = unwritten_r + 1 }
                                    if cas_alias == 1 {
                                        aliased_r = aliased_r + 1
                                    }
                                }
                                if pending == 4 { n_mrr_r = n_mrr_r + 1 }
                            }
                            pending = 0
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // ---------------------------------------------------------------- read drive
        // A burst starts on the clock its first DQS rise is due; a 2 tCK static preamble comes
        // before it unless the previous burst ends right then.
        if rd_st == 0 || rd_st == 3 {
            if rq_due == 1 {
                rd_st = 2
                rd_b = 0
                rd_sub = 1
                rd_line = h_line
                rd_kind = h_kind
                rd_ok0 = h_ok0
                rd_ok1 = h_ok1
                rd_cor0 = h_cor0
                rd_cor1 = h_cor1
                rd_mrv = h_mrv
                rq_head = rq_head + 1
                rq_n = if rd_cas == 1 && rq_full == 0 { rq_n } else { rq_n - 1 }
                dqs_out_r = 1
                dqs_oe_r = 1
                dq_out_r = h_data
                dq_oe_r = 1
            } else {
                if rq_pre_due == 1 {
                    rd_st = 1
                    dqs_out_r = 0
                    dqs_oe_r = 1
                    dq_oe_r = 0
                } else {
                    if rd_st == 3 {
                        if rd_sub == half_ck[7:0] {
                            rd_st = 0
                            dqs_oe_r = 0
                        } else {
                            rd_sub = rd_sub + 1
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        } else {
            if rd_st == 1 {
                if rq_due == 1 {
                    rd_st = 2
                    rd_b = 0
                    rd_sub = 1
                    rd_line = h_line
                    rd_kind = h_kind
                    rd_ok0 = h_ok0
                rd_ok1 = h_ok1
                rd_cor0 = h_cor0
                rd_cor1 = h_cor1
                    rd_mrv = h_mrv
                    rq_head = rq_head + 1
                    rq_n = if rd_cas == 1 && rq_full == 0 { rq_n } else { rq_n - 1 }
                    dqs_out_r = 1
                    dq_out_r = h_data
                    dq_oe_r = 1
                }
            } else {
                // rd_st == 2: 16 beats, each half a tCK
                if rd_b == 15 && rd_sub == half_ck[7:0] && rq_due == 1 {
                    // seamless: the next burst's beat 0 follows beat 15 directly
                    rd_b = 0
                    rd_sub = 1
                    rd_line = h_line
                    rd_kind = h_kind
                    rd_ok0 = h_ok0
                rd_ok1 = h_ok1
                rd_cor0 = h_cor0
                rd_cor1 = h_cor1
                    rd_mrv = h_mrv
                    rq_head = rq_head + 1
                    rq_n = if rd_cas == 1 && rq_full == 0 { rq_n } else { rq_n - 1 }
                    dqs_out_r = 1
                    dq_out_r = h_data
                } else {
                    if rd_sub == half_ck[7:0] {
                        rd_sub = 1
                        if rd_b == 15 {
                            // postamble: DQS held low for half a tCK, DQ released
                            rd_st = 3
                            dq_oe_r = 0
                            dqs_out_r = 0
                        } else {
                            rd_b = rd_b + 1
                            dqs_out_r = if rd_b[0] == 1 { 1 } else { 0 }
                            dq_out_r = rd_data_next
                        }
                    } else {
                        rd_sub = rd_sub + 1
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    dq_out = if wl_mode == 1 { {fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[1], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0], fb_v[0]} } else { dq_skewed }
    dq_oe = dram_dq_oe
    dqs_out = dqs_out_r
    dqs_oe = dqs_oe_r
    errors = errors_r
    err_code = err_code_r
    err_cycle = err_cycle_r
    contention = cont_r
    dq_viol = viol_r
    aliased = aliased_r
    unwritten = unwritten_r
    n_act = n_act_r
    n_wr = n_wr_r
    n_rd = n_rd_r
    n_mrw = n_mrw_r
    n_mrr = n_mrr_r
    n_ref = n_ref_r
    ref_owed = ref_debt
    n_zq = n_zq_r
    t_ck_clks = t_ck
    mr2_o = mr2
    mr13_o = mr13
}
